cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code, please cite the archived release and the thesis it accompanies.
title: SALGINTR 2025/26 analysis code
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, pseudocode and computational specifications for the SALGINTR study, a
  physician-based digital participatory surveillance system for influenza-like illness in Türkiye,
  covering the 2025/26 season (ISO weeks 40/2025 to 20/2026). Includes the variable codebook and the
  aberration-detection ensemble implemented from published detector definitions. The analysis dataset
  is not distributed; see the data-availability statement in README.md.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/salgintr/SALGINTR-2025-2026-analysis
keywords:
  - participatory surveillance
  - influenza-like illness
  - syndromic surveillance
  - aberration detection
  - recurrent-event analysis
  - reproducible research
authors:
  - name: SALGINTR study
    website: https://github.com/salgintr

